# Chrome extension (feed collector)

## Purpose

**`chrome-extension/prothomalo-feed-collector/`** — Manifest V3 extension that collects Prothom Alo (and optional custom) RSS feeds into **JSON/CSV** under `~/Downloads/prothomalo-feed/`. Admins upload those files into Shorup via **file** ingest mode (`POST /api/v1/admin/sources/{id}/import` — proxied as **`POST /api/admin/sources/[id]/import`**). Not part of the Next.js or FastAPI bundles.

## Layout

- **`manifest.json`** — permissions (`downloads`, `alarms`, `storage`, `<all_urls>` for arbitrary RSS URLs)
- **`background.js`** — scheduled collection via `chrome.alarms`
- **`popup.*`** — manual **Collect now**
- **`options.*`** — section feed checklist, extra RSS URLs, schedule, export format
- **`lib/`** — `collect.js`, `feeds.js`, `feed-parser.js`, `export-local.js`, `schedule.js`, `prothomalo-sections.js`, `storage.js`

## Conventions

- Vanilla JS (no bundler); bump **`manifest.json` version** when shipping UX fixes so testers know to **Reload** on `chrome://extensions`
- JSON article shape should stay compatible with **`feed_file_import.py`** — at minimum `title` + `link`/`url`; optional `imageUrl`/`image_url`, `pubDate`, excerpt fields
- Duplicates merged by article URL in the collector; backend dedupes by URL on import (same clustering path as live RSS via **`persist_feed_items`**)
- User-facing setup: **`chrome-extension/prothomalo-feed-collector/README.md`** (install, schedule, section RSS table, file naming)

## Product link

1. Extension saves e.g. `stories.json` or merged export.
2. Admin **Sources** → create **file** mode source (or upload on existing file-mode row) → later **PATCH** live RSS URL to switch to automatic pulls without losing articles.

Do not store admin API keys or backend URLs in the extension — upload is manual through the admin UI.
